      "side": 1,
      "message": "This forwards a request nobody authenticated and relies on the next handler to reject it. A chunk-size failure keeps the real method, URI and headers, so any handler other than HTTPServerSession that skips the decoderResult check would act on it. Could the auth handler answer the 400/414/431 itself (for example by reusing HTTPServerSession.statusOf), or at least document this contract on this public class?",
      "revId": "abcb1e337e323551a2347e1b6e2a41e255d6faca",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
