      "writtenOn": "2026-10-29T10:42:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Bodies are aggregated before authentication, and Netty advertises 100 concurrent streams, so this default lets an unauthenticated client pin about 100 MiB per HTTP/2 connection instead of 1.6 MiB today. It is documented, but should every deployment pay that by default? Would a smaller default (say 256 KiB), or a lower maxConcurrentStreams, still cover the topology use case? Something to considder.",
      "revId": "abcb1e337e323551a2347e1b6e2a41e255d6faca",
      "serverId": "7fc14799-209e-464c-9743-7a06c2c21a81"
